{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הראך את אשו הגדולה", :translit "hera'cha et esho ha-gedolah", :gloss "He showed you His great fire"} {:he "ותחת כי אהב את אבותיך", :translit "u-techat ki ahav et avotecha", :gloss "and because He loved your fathers"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: juxtaposition of adjacent verses drives the inference"}], :frame {:text "The verse states 'He showed you His great fire' and is immediately followed by 'and because He loved your fathers.' The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition (semikhah) as causal: the revelation of the great fire to Moses was granted in the merit of the patriarchs. The concept that the fathers' merit sustains Israel is rooted in Deuteronomy 4:37 itself, which states 'because He loved your fathers, He chose their seed after them,' and in Leviticus 26:42, where God promises to remember His covenant with Jacob, Isaac, and Abraham.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 4:37" "Leviticus 26:42"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: juxtaposition of adjacent verses drives the inference", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:03.741741371Z", :model "glm-5.2"}